-- Migration 15: takeover-resistant spray source (Phase 6 tuning r8). A takeover (a sprayed account that
-- later signs in from the address) must not remove the source.

ALTER TABLE spray_sources ADD COLUMN sprayed_users BIGINT;
ALTER TABLE spray_sources ADD COLUMN takeover_users BIGINT;

COMMENT ON TABLE spray_sources IS 'Password-spray source addresses per tenant, rewritten by every profile run. For each (address, user) with an interactive credential failure from the address (the credential_failure_codes list; a sign-in of unknown kind counts as interactive), the user is EXCUSED only if they have a known success (error_code 0) from that address either BEFORE their first credential failure there (the address was already theirs) or within 30 minutes AFTER one of their failures there (a typo correction). Every other failed user is a SPRAYED user, including users whose only successes there come later (the takeover pattern). An address is a source when at least 5 users were sprayed AND the sprayed users outnumber the excusing users (distinct users with a known success from the address, minus the late-takeover users). An office NAT or VPN egress, where users mistype and succeed within minutes or have signed in for days, is not a source; a proxy that sprays and takes accounts over stays one. The address type does not matter and no GeoIP is needed. Rules read it through the tenant scope like any tenant-aware table.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN spray_sources.failed_only_users IS 'Distinct users with a credential failure from this address and no known success from it anywhere in the case (context only; the source condition uses sprayed_users).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN spray_sources.sprayed_users IS 'Distinct users with a credential failure from this address that is not excused (no success before their first failure there and none within 30 minutes after one of their failures).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN spray_sources.takeover_users IS 'Sprayed users who have a known success from this address (a success later than 30 minutes after their failures: the account was taken over).';

COMMENT ON TABLE cloud_services IS 'Tenant-wide cloud services per tenant, rewritten by every profile run (after spray_sources), one row per (application, hosting ASN), established from the WHOLE case: at least 5 distinct users have known successes (error_code 0, interactive or not) to the application from that hosting ASN (ip_intel.is_hosting) on at least 3 distinct UTC days AND those sign-ins are at least 80% of the application''s known successes. The pair does NOT qualify when any of its users has a credential failure (interactive or unknown kind, the credential_failure_codes list) from a spray source of the tenant, or when any credential failure to the application comes from that ASN: accounts taken from a spray, or typed wrongly on a VPS first, never make their VPS a connector. Residual: 5+ phished (not sprayed) accounts used from one VPS on one application for 3+ days with no failures are excused. Typical case: a third-party SaaS connector whose public-cloud backend signs users in on their behalf. A rule excuses every sign-in to that application from that same ASN; a spray-source sign-in and a UAL UserLoggedIn always count. No application name or id is involved.';
